# {{ app_name }} — guide for AI assistants

This app is built on the Modulus framework and the Modulus UI framework (the `Synvro.Modulus.*` packages).
Read this file first. For the UI components and patterns, read `.claude/skills/modulus-ui/SKILL.md`.

## Layout

- `src/API/{{ root_namespace }}.Api` — the API host: modules, data, and the endpoints.
{{ if ui_engine == "blazor" }}- `src/Web/{{ root_namespace }}.Web` — the Blazor host: pages in `Components/Pages/<Module>/<Entities>`, the shell in `Components/Layout`, the menu contributors in `Components/Navigation/Menu`, the typed API clients in `Services/ApiClients`, the client registration in `Services/ApiClientExtensions.cs`.
{{ else }}- `src/Web/{{ root_namespace }}.Web` — the {{ if ui_engine == "mvc" }}MVC{{ else }}Razor Pages{{ end }} host: {{ if ui_engine == "mvc" }}controllers in `Controllers/<Module>`, views in `Views/<Entities>`{{ else }}pages in `Pages/<Module>/<Entities>`{{ end }}, the menu contributors in `Components/Navigation/Menu`, the typed API clients in `Services/ApiClients`, the client registration in `Services/ApiClientExtensions.cs`.
{{ end }}- `.modulus.json` — written by `modulus app`; it records the UI engine (`{{ ui_engine }}`) for later `modulus` commands.

## Working rules

- The UI engine is **{{ ui_engine }}**. Use the components and patterns for that engine (see the skill). Do not mix engines.
- Build and run the web host with `dotnet run --project src/Web/{{ root_namespace }}.Web`. Run the API host the same way, in another terminal. The web host calls the API over HTTP.
- Scaffold with the CLI, not by hand, where a command exists: `modulus ui add-component`, `modulus ui create-form-from-entity`, `modulus ui create-crud`, `modulus ui create-dashboard`, `modulus ui add-chart`. Pass `--dry-run` first to see the files.
- Menu items come from an `IMenuContributor`. Set `Href` without a leading slash (`customers`, not `/customers`).
- Theme and layout come from `Modulus:Theme` in `appsettings.json`.
- Keep every `Synvro.Modulus.*` package at the same version.
{{ if use_auth }}- Pages need a signed-in user, except `/Account`. Sign-in uses the BFF session; the tokens stay on the server.
{{ else }}- The app has no sign-in yet. Add authentication before exposing it to users.
{{ end }}
## Before you finish a change

- `dotnet build` succeeds.
- Run the web host and open the page you changed. Check it in both light and dark mode.
- For a form that saves, submit it once with bad input and once with good input.
